# FIX-P12-3 — CFN-direct CustomResource (kills F-3 fail-closed breach + IAM race)
# Executed: 2026-07-18
# Status: CLOSED

## Root Cause (F-3)
AwsCustomResource uses Lambda.invoke SDK call → HTTP 200 even when invoked function
errors (FunctionError header). CR reports SUCCESS to CFN → deploy goes green on failed
seed. ACC-5 (fail-closed propagates to deploy) falsified by direct observation.

## Fix
1. Created `services/iso-kb-seeder/src/cfn-handler.ts`:
   - CloudFormation cfn-response protocol (HTTPS PUT to pre-signed ResponseURL)
   - Create/Update → seed() → SUCCESS (Data: ContentHash, ChunksIndexed) or FAILED (Reason)
   - Delete → no-op SUCCESS (index outlives stack)
   - Internal deadline ~280s (Promise.race) — never hits CFN 1-hour timeout
   - Response ALWAYS sent (try/catch around everything)

2. Refactored `services/iso-kb-seeder/src/handler.ts`:
   - Exported `seed()` function (no event dependency)
   - cfn-handler.ts calls seed() on Create/Update

3. CDK `infra/lib/ai-stack.ts`:
   - Entry point changed: cfn-handler.ts
   - AwsCustomResource replaced with cdk.CustomResource:
     serviceToken: isoKbSeederFn.functionArn, resourceType: 'Custom::IsoKbSeed',
     properties: { SourceHash: fingerprint }
   - Lambda permission for cloudformation.amazonaws.com to invoke
   - Dependencies on access policies + applyTemplateTrigger preserved

4. Unit tests (`cfn-handler.test.ts`, 5 tests):
   - Create SUCCESS with Data (seeded)
   - Update SUCCESS (skipped)
   - Create FAILED with reason (template absent)
   - Delete no-op (seed not called)
   - Response always sent on unexpected error

5. handler.unit.test.ts: updated to call seed() instead of handler(event)

## Evidence
- tsc --noEmit: exit 0
- vitest run cfn-handler.test.ts: 5 passed (5)
- vitest run handler.unit.test.ts: 4 passed (4)
- Full suite: 1085 passed | 3 skipped (102 files), exit 0
- cdk synth --all: exit 0
